Part of the future developments roadmap set in the original project's research report mentioned a shift from insecure http static website hosting
over to https. This will be done by placing the Amazon S3 bucket behind Cloudfront, whatever that means lol. The required steps will be documented below.

1.  Getting started with a cloudfront distribution: Navigate to Cloudfront, select create distribution.
- Named the distribution
- Selected the assets bucket as the S3 origin for the distribution.
- Configured CloudFront's WAF to protect against attacks.
- Enabled DDoS protection: AWS learns your application pattern, letting it distinguish between standard traffic surges and attacks.
- Setting the distribution origin to the S3 bucket automatically creates a corresponding origin access policy (OAC). 
- Had to set the root object to index.html so cloudfront knows how to access the application's assets.


